MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and To Be Loved feel like natural next choices because polished vocals and familiar standards connect with what I enjoyed about Stages, A Musical Affair, and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "That's Christmas To Me connects with my Christmas listening, while Eagles: The Very Best Of and Storyteller reflect my interest in familiar melodies and some country music, even though those are weaker choices for this session."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour, 25, and Oscd Ad Adele 21 offer expressive singing, but that alone does not give me the standards and classical crossover feeling I want right now.",
    "1989 feels distant from my current listening mood, and Django and Jimmie does not have a clear enough connection to what appealed to me about my previous country selections."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in strong singers seems to have been stretched into a broad interest in contemporary pop and soul, when the style and repertoire matter to me.",
    "My past holiday and country listening seems to count as a reason to choose more of either now, although those interests depend on the occasion and the particular album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The recurring appeal of crossover vocals, musical standards, and polished ensemble singing deserves more attention than a general similarity between vocal albums.",
    "My latest choice of relaxing classical music suggests that a calmer listening experience matters now; an album can fit an older interest without being what I want this time."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices recognize my interest in melodic vocal music but stretch it too broadly beyond the standards, crossover singing, and calmer listening I currently prefer."
}
